From: MiMoCode <mimocode@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Enable 48MP capture mode for OV48B sensor

Change the camera capture mode from 12MP binning to 48MP full resolution
for the OV48B sensor on Redmi 10X 5G (atom).

The OV48B sensor supports 8000x6000 (48MP) in custom4 mode, but the
default driver only uses 4000x3000 (12MP) binning mode. This patch
changes the capture scenario to use custom4 mode instead.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/common/v1_1/ov48bofilm_mipi_raw/ov48bofilmmipiraw_Sensor.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/common/v1_1/ov48bofilm_mipi_raw/ov48bofilmmipiraw_Sensor.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/common/v1_1/ov48bofilm_mipi_raw/ov48bofilmmipiraw_Sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/common/v1_1/ov48bofilm_mipi_raw/ov48bofilmmipiraw_Sensor.c
@@ -1456,7 +1456,7 @@ static kal_uint32 control(enum MSDK_SCENARIO_ID_ENUM scenario_id, MSDK_SENSOR_E
 		preview(image_window, sensor_config_data);
 		break;
 	case MSDK_SCENARIO_ID_CAMERA_CAPTURE_JPEG:
-		capture(image_window, sensor_config_data);
+		custom4(image_window, sensor_config_data);
 		break;
 	case MSDK_SCENARIO_ID_VIDEO_PREVIEW:
 		normal_video(image_window, sensor_config_data);
